  "question": {
    "text": "Two charges <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>q</mi></math> are separated by a distance ‘<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>’ in air. At a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> from charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math>, the resultant electric field is zero. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is :"
